.TH SECRET 1 "2026-11-26" "secret 2.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
secret \- value-minimizing secret manager for configured aliases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B secret
.IR command " [" options "] [" arguments ]
.RI [ -- ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B secret
reads and writes secrets that are stored in a vault (Bitwarden, 1Password or
the macOS Keychain) and addressed through short aliases declared in config
files.
.PP
Aliases are merged from three scopes, later scopes winning:
.RS 4
.TP
.B project
.I ./.secret.json
walked up from the current directory, committed to the repository.
.TP
.B global
.I ~/.config/secret/config.json
(override the directory with
.BR SECRET_CONFIG_DIR ),
shared by every directory.
.TP
.B local
.I ./.secret.local.json
machine-specific overrides, never committed.
.RE
.PP
Values never live in a config:
.I item
names the vault item and
.I field
picks the value inside it.
An alias may also carry
.IR backend ,
.IR expect
(a value rule) and
.IR expiresAt .
.PP
By design the tool prints as little as possible: listings carry metadata only,
.B get
prints exactly one value, and
.B run
scrubs every known value out of the child's output.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Reading
.TP
.B status
Report whether the vault is authenticated and unlocked, and what to run next.
.TP
.B list
List configured aliases (alias, item, field). Created dates are read from the
vault only on a terminal.
.TP
.BR get " " alias
Print one value. Fails with the fix when the alias is unknown, the item is
missing, or the alias has expired.
.TP
.BR totp " " alias
Print the current one-time code for that item.
.TP
.BR id " " alias
Print the resolved vault item id.
.TP
.BR source " " alias " [" url ]
Print the source URL stored on the item, or set it.
.TP
.BR search " " term
Find aliases by alias, item or environment variable name.
.TP
.BI print " [" scope ]
Show aliases in
.IR project " (default), " global " or " local ;
.B \-\-all
merges the scopes.
.TP
.BR unaliased " [" \-\-json ]
List vault items under
.B global/
that no alias declares. Reads still resolve them by name.
.TP
.BR history " [" \-\-json ]
Show the last commands and their targets, never values.
.TP
.BR recent " [" \-\-json ]
Show the aliases used most recently.
.TP
.BR audit " [" count "] [" \-\-json ]
Show the audit trail (caller, reason, outcome, directory) from
.IR ~/.local/state/secret/audit.log .
.SS Writing
.TP
.BI set " [" alias ] [" options ]
Prompt for a value and write it to the vault, creating the item and the config
entry when the alias is new.
.TP
.BI edit " " alias " [" options ]
Change the item name, value, source, notes, tags, value rule
.RB ( \-\-expect )
or backend override
.RB ( \-\-backend )
in place.
.TP
.BR rotate " " alias
Generate a new password and overwrite the item.
.TP
.BR rm " " alias
Delete the vault item (the config entry stays).
.TP
.BR unset " " alias
Remove the alias from its config (the item stays).
.TP
.BR mv " " alias " " new-alias
Rename an alias in its config.
.TP
.BR pin " " alias
Replace the item name in the config with the resolved item id.
.TP
.BR adopt " " alias " [" options ]
Declare an alias for an item that already exists, without re-entering its
value. Defaults to
.I global/<alias>
with
.B \-\-global
and
.I <folder>/<alias>
for a project config.
.TP
.BR prune " [" \-\-dry-run ]
Drop config entries whose vault items no longer exist.
.TP
.BR init " [" alias ... ]
Scaffold a project config.
.SS Using secrets
.TP
.BI env " [" options ]
Print a dotenv file for the project aliases.
.B \-\-export
prints shell exports,
.B \-\-output FILE
writes it atomically (mode 0600),
.B \-\-merge
upserts keys,
.B \-\-diff
shows key-level changes without values.
.TP
.BR run " [--] " command " [" args ... ]
Run a command with the project aliases in its environment, scrubbing every
injected value from its stdout and stderr.
.TP
.BR generate " [" \-\-kind " " kind ]
Print one generated value:
.IR password " (default), " token ", " hex ", " base64 ", " uuid " or " passphrase .
Nothing is stored.
.TP
.BR mcp
Serve secrets over the Model Context Protocol on stdin/stdout. Tools:
.BR secret_list ", " secret_check ", " secret_status ", " secret_scan " and " secret_run .
No tool returns a value;
.B secret_run
injects values into a child and returns its output with the values replaced by
.IR [scrubbed] .
.SS Integrations
.TP
.BR git-credential " " get|store|erase
Git credential helper. Maps a host (or host/path) from
.B integrations.git
to an alias and answers
.IR username " and " password .
An unmapped host exits 0 so git falls through to the next helper.
.TP
.BR docker-credential " " get|list|store|erase
Docker credential helper for
.BR integrations.docker .
.SS Health
.TP
.BR lint " [" \-\-json ]
Validate configs offline: missing items, dotenv-key collisions, rule syntax.
.TP
.BR doctor " [" \-\-json ] [" \-\-ci ]
Resolve every alias through its own backend and report
.IR ok ", " missing ", " invalid ", " expired " or " mismatch
(a value that breaks its
.IR expect " rule)."
.B check
is the same command in CI mode: non-interactive, problems only, exit 1.
.SS Session
.TP
.BR unlock " [" \-\-store | \-\-helper ]
Obtain a fresh session; stores it, or caches it behind Touch ID.
.TP
.B lock
Lock the vault, clear the stored session and stop the daemon.
.TP
.B pull
Refresh the local vault cache from the server.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config FILE
Use FILE instead of the discovered project config.
.TP
.BI \-\-env " NAME"
Environment overrides within a config (default:
.IR prod ).
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FILE"
With
.BR env :
write the dotenv there atomically, mode 0600.
.TP
.BR \-\-export ", " \-\-merge ", " \-\-diff " ( " \-\-dry ", " \-\-dry-run )
With
.BR env :
shell exports, upsert, or report key-level changes without values.
.TP
.BR \-\-required " a,b " / " \-\-optional " a,b"
With
.BR env " or " run :
fail unless these aliases resolve, or warn and skip them.
.TP
.BR \-\-global ", " \-g
Operate on the global config.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Machine-readable output where a command supports it.
.TP
.BR \-\-copy
With
.BR get " or " totp :
put the value on the clipboard instead of stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-force ", " \-f
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-generate
With
.BR set :
generate the value instead of prompting.
.TP
.BR \-\-field " FIELD"
Value field inside the item (default
.IR password ).
.TP
.BR \-\-name " NAME", " \-\-notes " TEXT", " \-\-source " URL", " \-\-type " login|secure-note", " \-\-expires-at " DATE", " \-\-tags " a,b"
With
.BR set " or " edit :
item metadata.
.TP
.B \-\-expect RULE
With
.BR edit " or " adopt :
a value rule.
.TP
.B \-\-backend NAME
With
.BR set ", " edit " or " adopt :
.IR bitwarden ", " 1password " or " keychain
for this alias.
.TP
.B \-\-allow-expired
With
.BR env " or " run :
inject an alias whose
.I expiresAt
has passed.
.TP
.B \-\-kind ", " \-\-length ", " \-\-words ", " \-\-separator ", " \-\-no-symbols
With
.BR generate :
what to produce.
.TP
.B \-\-caller " NAME" / " \-\-reason " TEXT"
Record who is calling and why in the audit log.
.TP
.B \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help, also per command
.RB ( "secret get --help" ).
.SH VALUE RULES
An alias may declare
.B expect
so a wrong-shaped value never reaches a command:
.PP
.nf
"PORT":    { "item": "app", "field": "port", "expect": "port" }
"API_URL": { "item": "app", "field": "url",  "expect": "url" }
"MODE":    { "item": "app", "field": "mode", "expect": "enum:dev,prod" }
"STRIPE":  { "item": "app", "field": "key",
             "expect": "string(startsWith=sk-)" }
.fi
.PP
Rules:
.BR string ", " nonempty ", " url ", " email ", " port ", " number ", " integer ", " boolean ", " json ", " base64 ", " uuid ", " enum:a,b
and
.BR "string(startswith=..." ", " "endswith=..." ", " "contains=..." ", " "length=N)" .
.B env
and
.B run
refuse a value that fails; the failure names the alias and the rule, never the
value.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SECRET_CONFIG_DIR
Directory holding the config, session and daemon state (default
.IR ~/.config/secret ).
.TP
.B SECRET_BACKEND
Force one backend for a single invocation.
.TP
.B SECRET_ONEPASSWORD_VAULT
Vault name for 1Password aliases that name a bare item.
.TP
.B SECRET_KEYCHAIN_SERVICE
Keychain service name (default
.IR dev.astahmer.secret ).
.TP
.B SECRET_DENY_PLAINTEXT_GET\fR=\fP1
Refuse
.B get
without
.BR \-\-copy ,
for shells an agent controls.
.TP
.B SECRET_CALLER ", " SECRET_REASON
Default audit attribution.
.TP
.B SECRET_AUDIT_FILE ", " SECRET_AUDIT_DIR
Move the audit log;
.B SECRET_NO_AUDIT\fR=\fP1
disables it.
.TP
.B SECRET_DAEMON\fR=\fP0
Do not use the background vault daemon.
.TP
.B SECRET_NO_BIOMETRICS\fR=\fP1
Never prompt for Touch ID.
.TP
.BR BW_SESSION ", " OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN
Sessions forwarded to the Bitwarden and 1Password CLIs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/secret/config.json
Global aliases, integrations and the default backend.
.TP
.I ./.secret.json ", " ./.secret.local.json
Project and machine-local aliases.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/secret/audit.log
Append-only JSONL audit trail, mode 0600, rotated at 5 MiB.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/secret/aliases
Alias cache used by shell completion.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success; 1 on a refused or failed operation, including
.B check
finding a problem, an expired alias reaching
.B env " or " run ,
and a
.B scan
hit. 2 from
.B scan
when nothing could be resolved to search for.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
secret status                                   # unlocked?
secret list                                     # aliases in this folder
secret get github-token | pbcopy                # one value
secret run -- npm test                          # inject + scrub output
secret generate --kind passphrase --words 5
secret adopt openai-key --global --expect nonempty
secret doctor --json | jq '.[] | select(.status != "ok")'
secret edit stripe --expect 'string(startsWith=sk-)'
.fi
.PP
Git helper:
.nf
git config --global credential.https://github.com.helper \
  '!secret git-credential'
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Aliases and metadata are committed; values never are.
.B secret mcp " and " secret run
are the supported way to give a program (or an agent) a credential without
handing over its plaintext.
.B scan
finds a value that leaked into a file and reports the file and alias only.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR git-credential (1),
.BR docker-login (1)
